rows=[(293, 'warmth-from-the-clay-oven', 'Warmth from the clay oven', 'The poem remembers warmth shared around a sister’s clay oven and the loss of that shelter. Show the modest source of heat in remembered use, without inventing the sister or siblings, and without reducing grief to a ruined oven.', 'Horizontal 3:2 intimate low-angle gouache and charcoal study of a simple small earthen clay cooking stove in a modest plain kitchen corner. Its lower fire opening glows softly red from a few embers, a flat dark iron griddle rests securely on the top supports with one irregular handmade flatbread cooking. Outer clay stays matte earth-brown, only the inside fire opening glows, never the whole clay body. One dim bare bulb outside frame supplies weak neutral room light, warm ember light reaches only adjacent stove edges. Crop scene closely with broad quieter shadow on one side; no person, hands, shrine, flame spectacle, stacked props, pristine commercial styling or ornamental decay. Roundness of stove and imperfect bread quietly echoes the children’s comparison. Physically coherent heat, weight and utensil placement.'), (299, 'the-pause-in-the-corridor', 'The pause in the corridor', 'The speaker waits for a teacher to turn back. The corridor after her passing can hold that suspended expectation without inventing her likeness or turning the title into a literal sunrise landscape.', 'Horizontal 3:2 very spare graphite and pale grey gouache architectural drawing. View along a short ordinary school corridor to an open classroom doorway at right mid-distance, the room beyond only an empty dim plane. A row of off-frame openings on left gives soft broad lateral daylight, not sharp repetitive sunbeams. Plain clean matte walls, slightly uneven floor tone; narrow chalk-white line of light at doorway jamb. Perspective coherent, corridor turns out of view rather than endless vanishing point. No person, silhouette, floating fabric, chalk props, books, text, school sign or period/location claims. Most of image quiet pale paper, selective pencil lines only at essential wall and floor joins. Expectant pause, a human absence rather than institutional menace.'), (302, 'kash-beside-the-receding-river', 'Kash beside the receding river', 'The poem’s distant village is felt through moonlit paddy and Kash beside a half-dried river. A spare riverbank fragment preserves that isolation without inventing village residents or assembling every scene in the poem.', 'Horizontal 3:2 soft hand-printed monotype with thin watercolor wash on warm opaque paper. Night view of a shallow receding river channel curving off-center across a broad exposed dull sandbank; a small uneven cluster of slender Kash grass with off-white feathery plumes grows from the near bank at left, some cropped and overlapping, modestly leaning with a breeze. Far bank low and nearly unarticulated; no mountains, village buildings, people, moon disk, boats, birds or reflective palace. Muted indigo, ash grey and quiet paper-white. Moonlight is implied by small soft pale accents on plumes and broken water, no bright silver highway. Plausible grass rooted in bank, narrow water channel lower than ground, selective marks with quiet dark and empty space.')]
items=[]
